---
const { contactEmail } = Astro.props;
const googlePrivacyUrl = 'https://policies.google.com/privacy';
const firebasePrivacyUrl = 'https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy';
const applePrivacyUrl = 'https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/';
const gsaPoliciesUrl = 'https://www.gsa.gov/website-information/website-policies';
const officialGsaAuctionsUrl = 'https://www.gsaauctions.gov/';
---

<div class="legal-content">
  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how Restart Apps ("we", "us", or "our") handles
      information when you use GSA Auction Finder (the "App" or "Service").
    </p>
    <p>
      The App is an independent auction-discovery tool. It is not affiliated with,
      endorsed by, or operated by the U.S. General Services Administration or the
      United States Government.
    </p>
    <p>
      The App helps users discover public GSA Auctions listings, search and filter
      downloaded listings, save listings and searches, compare listings, save ZIP
      locations, receive best-effort alerts, and open official listings for bidding
      or buying.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Listings, Searches, and Network Requests</h2>
    <p>
      The App retrieves public auction listings from GSA's API and obtains photos,
      descriptions, bidding information, documents, and other listing details from
      GSA website services and hosting providers, including Amazon S3. These
      providers receive normal network information such as IP address and requests
      identifying the listings or files you open.
    </p>
    <p>
      Search and filter matching use downloaded listings on your device. We do not
      operate a backend that receives your saved searches, personal notes, watchlist,
      saved ZIP locations, or comparison selections.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Information Stored on Your Device</h2>
    <p>
      The App stores saved listings, personal notes, saved searches, saved ZIP
      locations, filters, notification preferences, alert history and baselines,
      onboarding state, theme settings, recently viewed listings, and cached
      subscription verification locally on your device.
    </p>
    <p>
      Auction information and images may be cached to improve loading and offline
      browsing. Recently Viewed keeps up to ten listing snapshots on your device.
      Comparison selections are temporary browsing state.
    </p>
    <p>
      The App does not currently offer app-managed accounts, sign-in, cloud sync,
      Firebase Authentication, Cloud Firestore, or Firebase Cloud Messaging.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Location, ZIP Areas, and Maps</h2>
    <p>
      If you choose a current-location feature and grant permission, the App uses
      device location to estimate a nearby supported ZIP-area location. Exact device
      coordinates remain transient and are not stored by our backend. You can enter
      and save ZIP codes instead, and you can revoke location permission in system
      settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      Listing maps use Google Maps on Android and Apple MapKit on iOS. Public
      property addresses may be sent to platform geocoding services to estimate a
      listing pin. Map and geocoding providers may process IP address, device
      information, usage, and diagnostics under their own policies. Map previews do
      not enable a user-location layer.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Advertising and Privacy Choices</h2>
    <p>
      The free version uses Google AdMob for banner, native, and app-open
      advertisements. Google and its advertising partners may process IP address,
      approximate location derived from IP, advertising or other app/device
      identifiers where permitted, device and operating-system details, ad views and
      interactions, diagnostics, and consent state to deliver and measure ads,
      prevent fraud, and improve their services.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google User Messaging Platform handles applicable advertising privacy messages
      and consent choices. Available choices depend on your region, device settings,
      and the configured consent message. Pro removes advertisements, but it does
      not disable analytics, crash reporting, listing requests, maps, subscriptions,
      or store services.
    </p>
    <p>
      The App does not currently request Apple's App Tracking Transparency permission.
      This does not mean advertising or analytics SDKs process no information.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Analytics and Crash Reporting</h2>
    <p>
      The App uses Google Analytics for Firebase and Firebase Crashlytics when
      Firebase is configured. Usage Analytics and Crash Reports are separate,
      optional controls in Settings &gt; Data &amp; Privacy and are off by default
      until you choose to enable them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics can process app-instance identifiers, device and app details, usage
      and engagement events, and approximate geographic information. Crashlytics can
      process crash reports, stack traces, installation identifiers, device and
      operating-system details, and diagnostic information.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not intentionally include exact device coordinates, API keys, personal
      notes, raw search text, GSA contact fields, full auction descriptions, or
      official listing URLs in custom telemetry.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Alerts, Notifications, and Calendar Reminders</h2>
    <p>
      Free and Pro alerts are evaluated using downloaded data and local saved-search
      or saved-listing state. Alert check times, update history, matching baselines,
      and delivery-health information are stored locally. Android and iOS background
      services and local notifications are best effort; we do not operate remote
      push monitoring for this App.
    </p>
    <p>
      Notification text can include listing titles, saved-search names, or detected
      changes and may appear on your lock screen according to your device settings.
      You can change notification permission in system settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      Add to Calendar passes a listing title, closing date or time, public property
      address, and official link to the system calendar editor. You decide whether
      to save the event. The App does not read your existing calendar events.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Purchases, Reviews, and Support</h2>
    <p>
      Apple App Store and Google Play handle subscriptions, billing, refunds, and
      payment information. The App receives product, transaction, and entitlement
      information needed to activate or restore Pro, but we do not receive full
      payment-card details. Store purchase history remains with the applicable
      store account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Review actions open the appropriate store listing when available. Reviews are
      handled by the store and may be public under your store profile.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you contact <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>, we
      receive your email address and the message or attachments you choose to send.
      We use that information to respond to support, billing-routing, legal, or
      privacy requests.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>The App relies on services that process data under their own terms and policies, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>GSA Auctions API, official GSA Auctions pages, and related hosting providers.</li>
      <li>Google Maps, Apple MapKit, platform geocoding, device location, notifications, calendar, browser, sharing, phone, and email services.</li>
      <li>Google AdMob and Google User Messaging Platform.</li>
      <li>Google Analytics for Firebase and Firebase Crashlytics, when enabled.</li>
      <li>Google Play Billing, Apple StoreKit, and the applicable app store.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Provider information:
      <a href={gsaPoliciesUrl}>GSA website policies</a>,
      <a href={googlePrivacyUrl}>Google Privacy Policy</a>,
      <a href={firebasePrivacyUrl}>Firebase privacy and security</a>, and
      <a href={applePrivacyUrl}>Apple Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Retention, Deletion, and Your Choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can remove saved listings, searches, ZIP locations, and personal notes in
      the App. Clearing app data where supported or deleting the App removes local
      app data, although operating-system backups or restores may retain or restore
      copies. Cached content may be evicted independently of saved records.
    </p>
    <p>
      Deleting local app data does not cancel a subscription, remove calendar events,
      erase store records or submitted reviews, or immediately delete information
      already processed by service providers. Manage subscriptions in the applicable
      store and calendar events in your calendar provider.
    </p>
    <p>
      Depending on your location, you may have rights to request access, correction,
      deletion, restriction, objection, a copy of personal information, or withdrawal
      of consent where applicable. Contact
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. We may need information
      to verify and locate a request, and we cannot retrieve local-only records from
      your device.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Official Sources, Children, Security, and Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Verify auction details, sale terms, condition, inspection, pickup, payment,
      and bidding requirements through <a href={officialGsaAuctionsUrl}>official GSA Auctions</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The App is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly seek
      personal information from children under 13.
    </p>
    <p>
      The App uses HTTPS for supported network services and platform storage
      protections, but no transmission or storage system is completely secure.
      Providers may process information in the United States or other countries
      under their applicable safeguards and policies.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may revise this policy as features or practices change. Questions may be
      sent to <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
